<worksheet>
    <title>Problem 20 - Written Homework - MTH 204</title>

<p>
        You should write up solutions neatly to all problems, making sure to
        show all your work and follow the homework policies (see Blackboard
        document for details).
        You will turn in the hand-written assignment in person during Wednesday
        class time.
        The solutions you turn in should be your own work and written in your
        own words.
        You cannot use any resources outside of discussing with your professor
        or classmates and/or your textbook.
        At the top of your first page of solutions, please list the names of any
        students who you worked with on the assignment.
        Don't forget to put your name at the top of the first page!
    </p>

        <!-- Question 20, Section 3.1 -->
        <exercise>
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Determine whether the following statements are true or false
                    and explain your reasoning.
                    If you use a proposition from the text, please refer to that
                    clearly by number and by a summary of what the proposition
                    tells you.
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task workspace="1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        If <m>A</m> is invertible, then the columns of <m>A</m>
                        are linearly independent.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1in"> 
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        If <m>A</m> is a square matrix whose diagonal entries
                        are all nonzero, then <m>A</m> is invertible.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        If <m>A</m> is a square matrix whose diagonal entries
                        are all nonzero, then <m>A</m> is invertible.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        If <m>A</m> is an invertible <m>n\times n</m> matrix,
                        then span of the columns of <m>A</m> is
                        <m>\mathbb{R}^{n}</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        If <m>A</m> is invertible, then there is a nonzero
                        solution to the homogeneous equation
                        <m>A{\vec x} = {\vec 0}</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        If <m>A</m> is an <m>n\times n</m> matrix and the
                        equation <m>A{\vec x}={\vec b}</m> has a solution for
                        every vector <m>{\vec b}</m>, then <m>A</m> is
                        invertible.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Using the figure, determine
                        <m>\{ {\vec a} \}_{\mathcal{B}}</m>,
                        <m>\{ {\vec b} \}_{\mathcal{B}}</m>, and
                        <m>\{ {\vec c} \}_{\mathcal{B}}</m> for the vectors
                        <md>
                            {\vec a} = \left[\begin{array}{r}-6 \\ 0\end{array}\right], \ {\vec b} = \left[\begin{array}{r}0 \\ -6\end{array}\right], \ {\vec c} = \left[\begin{array}{r}4 \\ 5\end{array}\right].
                        </md>
                        Again, write at least one sentence that explains how you
                        determined your results.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </exercise>
</worksheet>